From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fbdevhw: a monochrome mode's color lengths are its depth

A mode that is neither TrueColor nor DirectColor was asked of fbdev with
red, green and blue eight bits long, as for a palette of 256 colors.  A
monochrome framebuffer describes its mode with a bit of each, so the
kernel changed the request or refused it, and the server gave up.  A mode
of fewer than eight bits a pixel now asks for lengths of its depth.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: N/A a one-bit panel
---
--- a/hw/xfree86/fbdevhw/fbdevhw.c
+++ b/hw/xfree86/fbdevhw/fbdevhw.c
@@ -158,6 +158,13 @@
         var->green.length = pScrn->weight.green;
         var->blue.length = pScrn->weight.blue;
     }
+    else if (pScrn->bitsPerPixel < 8) {
+        /* A monochrome or few-color framebuffer: a pixel's bits are its
+           depth, as fbdev describes such a mode to us. */
+        var->red.length = pScrn->bitsPerPixel;
+        var->green.length = pScrn->bitsPerPixel;
+        var->blue.length = pScrn->bitsPerPixel;
+    }
     else {
         var->red.length = 8;
         var->green.length = 8;
